WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:38.070
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:38.340 --> 01:43.930
[Small Town Remedy]

3
01:44.100 --> 01:46.940
[Episode 13]

4
01:53.590 --> 01:54.520
What do you mean?

5
01:55.070 --> 01:57.070
So this is our last dinner together.

6
01:58.280 --> 01:59.940
Do you have to put it like that?

7
02:02.840 --> 02:04.560
I shouldn't have bothered asking you to come back.

8
02:04.560 --> 02:07.090
You're leaving again after such a short time.

9
02:12.240 --> 02:13.900
Where are you going this time?

10
02:14.710 --> 02:15.910
Haven't decided yet.

11
02:18.000 --> 02:20.520
Basically somewhere in the South, eh?

12
02:23.750 --> 02:24.480
Pretty much.

13
02:32.110 --> 02:33.120
Have you noticed?

14
02:33.590 --> 02:35.120
Summer here is pretty nice.

15
02:35.430 --> 02:37.290
It's not as hot as it is down South.

16
02:47.960 --> 02:49.490
I should probably warn you.

17
02:50.360 --> 02:52.120
If you come back next time,

18
02:52.310 --> 02:53.710
give me a heads-up first.

19
02:53.800 --> 02:55.360
I'll be very busy then.

20
02:55.360 --> 02:56.430
I'm job-hunting right now, remember?

21
02:56.430 --> 02:58.290
I'll be swamped with work by then.

22
02:59.079 --> 03:00.120
I'll be swamped.

23
03:00.120 --> 03:01.590
Y-You might not even get to see me.

24
03:01.590 --> 03:02.240
Maybe...

25
03:02.240 --> 03:04.030
Maybe I won't have time to see you.

26
03:04.030 --> 03:05.630
Let me know in advance, okay?

27
03:05.910 --> 03:07.190
Fine, Boss Liu.

28
03:07.630 --> 03:10.160
I'll let you know before I come back next time.

29
03:19.840 --> 03:21.500
I just remembered something.

30
03:21.590 --> 03:22.310
I just remembered.

31
03:22.310 --> 03:24.030
Do you remember when we were kids?

32
03:24.030 --> 03:25.240
Every time you were about to leave,

33
03:25.240 --> 03:27.040
you'd secretly cry in your room.

34
03:27.430 --> 03:28.190
Remember?

35
03:28.680 --> 03:30.150
You must have your wires crossed.

36
03:30.150 --> 03:30.960
When did I ever cry?

37
03:30.960 --> 03:32.079
Oh, cut it out.

38
03:32.360 --> 03:34.000
You and Mom,

39
03:34.470 --> 03:36.240
each hiding in your own room, crying.

40
03:36.240 --> 03:37.680
I saw it several times.

41
03:38.840 --> 03:40.470
But I do admit one thing.

42
03:41.840 --> 03:43.440
You really are a lot like Mom.

43
03:45.120 --> 03:46.320
Very strong-minded.

44
03:47.150 --> 03:49.120
Especially when something happens,

45
03:49.120 --> 03:51.920
neither of you tells anyone. You just tough it out.

46
04:00.750 --> 04:02.190
When Mom was sick...

47
04:04.960 --> 04:07.420
she wouldn't let me tell you, no matter what.

48
04:13.470 --> 04:14.630
That's quite funny.

49
04:15.030 --> 04:16.000
I stayed with Mom

50
04:16.000 --> 04:17.040
all those years,

51
04:17.040 --> 04:18.190
yet I didn't turn out like her.

52
04:18.190 --> 04:19.190
You did.

53
04:19.560 --> 04:20.510
How come?

54
04:23.600 --> 04:24.480
How come?

55
04:25.310 --> 04:27.680
You take after Dad, that's why.

56
04:32.190 --> 04:33.270
What was Dad like?

57
04:37.920 --> 04:39.380
He had a good personality.

58
04:39.720 --> 04:40.920
Always cheerful.

59
04:46.830 --> 04:47.830
That explains it.

60
04:48.630 --> 04:49.159
I've always

61
04:49.159 --> 04:50.720
wondered why I'm so lovable.

62
04:50.720 --> 04:52.180
Turns out I take after Dad.

63
04:52.630 --> 04:53.360
That's good.

64
04:57.480 --> 04:59.409
But you used to cry a lot as a kid too.

65
04:59.560 --> 05:00.680
You cried a lot as a kid,

66
05:00.680 --> 05:01.800
and you still do.

67
05:01.830 --> 05:03.830
Once you start, you just can't stop.

68
05:05.120 --> 05:05.630
Wait.

69
05:07.120 --> 05:07.920
How come...

70
05:07.950 --> 05:08.870
How come I...

71
05:08.920 --> 05:10.430
c-cry a lot now?

72
05:11.510 --> 05:13.310
Y-You have plenty of flaws too.

73
05:13.310 --> 05:14.070
You're annoying.

74
05:14.070 --> 05:14.920
You're the annoying type,

75
05:14.920 --> 05:15.680
through and through.

76
05:15.680 --> 05:18.040
You've been annoying since childhood,

77
05:18.040 --> 05:19.160
and somehow you've gotten

78
05:19.160 --> 05:20.890
even more annoying as an adult.

79
05:21.000 --> 05:21.600
I'm telling you,

80
05:21.600 --> 05:22.720
I find you so irritating now.

81
05:22.720 --> 05:24.120
You have no idea how much.

82
05:24.120 --> 05:25.390
Can you tell that I find you annoying?

83
05:25.390 --> 05:25.800
J-Just

84
05:25.800 --> 05:27.240
seeing you every day drives me up the wall.

85
05:27.240 --> 05:28.160
I-I really...

86
05:28.160 --> 05:30.040
I-I can barely...

87
05:31.040 --> 05:32.110
s-stand being

88
05:32.110 --> 05:32.680
around you anymore.

89
05:32.680 --> 05:33.950
H-Hurry up and leave.

90
05:53.830 --> 05:55.290
If you ever leave Fucheng,

91
05:56.600 --> 05:57.730
you can come find me.

92
06:00.990 --> 06:07.910
♪ Some say goodbye so easily ♪

93
06:03.240 --> 06:04.040
Forget it.

94
06:07.190 --> 06:07.990
I'm not going.

95
06:08.480 --> 06:09.570
I'm not going anywhere.

96
06:09.570 --> 06:15.390
♪ Yet take forever to let go ♪

97
06:11.390 --> 06:12.990
Staying here is pretty nice.

98
06:18.550 --> 06:25.510
♪ Some smile as they close the door ♪

99
06:24.720 --> 06:25.850
Don't just eat meat.

100
06:26.330 --> 06:32.750
♪ Yet turn away with tears in their eyes ♪

101
06:44.600 --> 06:45.390
Huang.

102
06:44.750 --> 06:47.150
[Xiamen Kaoliang Liquor]

103
06:46.040 --> 06:47.120
Although we have

104
06:47.120 --> 06:49.159
different personalities, don't see eye to eye,

105
06:49.159 --> 06:51.560
and probably won't see each other again...

106
06:52.360 --> 06:53.159
Um, well...

107
06:53.430 --> 06:54.600
This is a type of sorghum liquor

108
06:54.600 --> 06:55.630
from Fujian.

109
06:55.830 --> 06:57.120
An older colleague of mine at my previous workplace

110
06:57.120 --> 06:58.050
really liked it,

111
06:58.390 --> 06:59.159
so I ordered

112
06:59.159 --> 07:00.430
a bottle online for you.

113
07:00.430 --> 07:01.360
Give it a try.

114
07:05.040 --> 07:06.000
Thank you then.

115
07:07.270 --> 07:08.070
Dr. Che.

116
07:08.720 --> 07:09.510
Here.

117
07:09.830 --> 07:10.690
This is for you.

118
07:11.600 --> 07:13.530
It's a reading list I put together,

119
07:13.600 --> 07:14.310
along with some papers

120
07:14.310 --> 07:15.430
whose research frameworks I think

121
07:15.430 --> 07:16.830
are worth learning from.

122
07:17.630 --> 07:18.430
And here...

123
07:18.720 --> 07:20.270
is the phone number of one of my classmates.

124
07:20.270 --> 07:21.120
He specializes in

125
07:21.120 --> 07:22.240
tutoring for doctoral exams and applications.

126
07:22.240 --> 07:23.500
He's really good at it.

127
07:24.190 --> 07:25.360
But he...

128
07:26.270 --> 07:27.600
and I don't really get along,

129
07:27.600 --> 07:29.600
so you don't need to mention my name.

130
07:29.830 --> 07:30.760
You're leaving?

131
07:35.070 --> 07:36.159
If you have any questions

132
07:36.159 --> 07:37.600
about anything on this list,

133
07:37.600 --> 07:39.159
just compile them all

134
07:39.159 --> 07:40.360
and send me a message.

135
07:42.070 --> 07:42.870
Thank you.

136
07:47.750 --> 07:49.190
When you go back to the South,

137
07:49.190 --> 07:50.720
take good care of yourself.

138
07:54.950 --> 07:56.480
"The fish roam the vast sea,

139
07:57.870 --> 08:00.470
and the birds soar through the boundless sky."

140
08:01.560 --> 08:02.620
I hate to see you go.

141
08:05.680 --> 08:06.880
But I'm happy for you.

142
08:10.590 --> 08:17.370
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to erase the past ♪

143
08:13.530 --> 08:18.930
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

144
08:19.290 --> 08:26.300
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

145
08:24.210 --> 08:26.440
[Buddhist Scriptures, Joss Paper, Coffins, Refrigerated casket]

146
08:26.460 --> 08:27.870
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

147
08:27.990 --> 08:30.940
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

148
08:31.530 --> 08:35.330
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

149
08:36.000 --> 08:44.030
♪ Maybe walking side by side for a while is enough ♪

150
08:45.630 --> 08:48.850
[Fortune]

151
08:46.100 --> 08:52.880
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to erase the past ♪

152
08:48.750 --> 08:49.550
Nice.

153
08:54.970 --> 09:01.860
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

154
09:03.630 --> 09:06.480
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

155
09:07.180 --> 09:10.970
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

156
09:11.460 --> 09:19.610
♪ Maybe walking side by side for a while is enough ♪

157
09:12.870 --> 09:13.670
San.

158
09:15.120 --> 09:15.720
I...

159
09:15.720 --> 09:17.850
I think I just saw Liu Zhengliang here.

160
09:18.240 --> 09:19.030
What?

161
09:22.670 --> 09:23.730
I don't see anyone.

162
09:26.200 --> 09:27.360
Patient Wang Zongqi's

163
09:27.360 --> 09:28.910
post-op recovery is normal.

164
09:28.910 --> 09:29.750
Still under observation,

165
09:29.750 --> 09:31.150
nothing special needed.

166
09:31.270 --> 09:32.930
That's the nursing handover.

167
09:33.000 --> 09:34.150
Over to the doctors.

168
09:34.390 --> 09:36.390
The nurses' handover was detailed,

169
09:36.480 --> 09:38.340
and the additions were thorough.

170
09:38.390 --> 09:39.320
One more thing:

171
09:39.630 --> 09:40.550
today is Chief Physician Liu's

172
09:40.550 --> 09:41.670
last shift.

173
09:41.670 --> 09:42.550
That's all.

174
10:09.360 --> 10:10.150
Are you really not going to give yourself

175
10:10.150 --> 10:11.320
a chance?

176
10:14.000 --> 10:16.200
Once he leaves, he will never come back.

177
10:18.600 --> 10:21.610
[Gastric Lavage Room] [ECG Room]

178
10:20.320 --> 10:21.120
Dr. Liu.

179
10:24.980 --> 10:27.220
[No smoking]

180
10:30.030 --> 10:32.840
[Quiet]

181
10:31.550 --> 10:32.470
Dr. Liu.

182
10:35.000 --> 10:35.790
Dr. Liu.

183
11:24.840 --> 11:25.720
That day,

184
11:26.270 --> 11:27.750
Zhang Jiao sat beside me

185
11:28.790 --> 11:29.840
and smiled at me.

186
11:33.630 --> 11:35.150
Only I knew

187
11:35.670 --> 11:37.030
that I walked away

188
11:37.720 --> 11:39.720
much more slowly than I'd imagined.

189
11:56.470 --> 12:04.270
[Yellow Zone]

190
11:58.630 --> 11:59.550
Dr. Liu.

191
12:01.910 --> 12:02.750
Um,

192
12:03.200 --> 12:04.670
we heard you're leaving.

193
12:05.150 --> 12:05.870
This is

194
12:05.870 --> 12:08.080
a small token of appreciation from my husband and me.

195
12:08.080 --> 12:10.600
We hope everything goes well for you in the future.

196
12:10.600 --> 12:11.750
I can't accept this.

197
12:13.600 --> 12:15.000
I'm not good with words,

198
12:15.200 --> 12:16.550
and I don't know how to express myself well.

199
12:16.550 --> 12:17.480
But I know

200
12:17.790 --> 12:19.000
that without you,

201
12:19.240 --> 12:21.000
Jiao wouldn't have made it this far,

202
12:21.000 --> 12:23.060
nor would she have recovered so well.

203
12:23.550 --> 12:24.270
Besides,

204
12:24.270 --> 12:24.790
you've helped us

205
12:24.790 --> 12:26.790
save a lot of money on medical bills.

206
12:28.150 --> 12:29.440
Today is your last day

207
12:29.440 --> 12:30.770
at Xiaoximen Hospital.

208
12:31.390 --> 12:32.240
Her dad and I

209
12:32.240 --> 12:34.360
didn't know what to get you.

210
12:34.750 --> 12:36.350
It's meant purely as thanks.

211
12:36.510 --> 12:37.510
We're just afraid that if we don't

212
12:37.510 --> 12:39.790
thank you now, we might not get another chance.

213
12:39.790 --> 12:40.840
Please accept it.

214
12:41.630 --> 12:42.670
The hospital has rules.

215
12:42.670 --> 12:44.070
I really can't accept it.

216
12:46.960 --> 12:47.360
Just...

217
12:47.360 --> 12:49.320
Just think of it as a gift from Jiao.

218
12:50.150 --> 12:53.350
You can buy yourself something to eat or drink on the road.

219
12:53.550 --> 12:54.550
Please accept it.

220
13:00.390 --> 13:01.080
Okay.

221
13:04.910 --> 13:05.720
I'm going.

222
13:21.060 --> 13:22.180
[Guide for Patients with Out-of-Area Insurance]

223
13:21.240 --> 13:22.440
Um, here.

224
13:22.180 --> 13:22.370
[Priority for acute stroke patients and patients aged 80 and older.]

225
13:22.440 --> 13:23.320
Please deposit this

226
13:23.320 --> 13:24.850
into Zhang Jiao's account.

227
13:25.080 --> 13:27.340
-Okay, Chief Physician Liu. -Thank you.

228
13:29.360 --> 13:32.000
[Thank you, Dr. Liu Zhengliang, for saving Zhang Jiao.]

229
13:32.000 --> 13:34.210
[May you always be safe and sound, and may everything go well for you.]

230
13:43.480 --> 13:44.870
He'll be right out.

231
13:57.080 --> 13:57.910
I can't take you to the station now.

232
13:57.910 --> 13:58.720
Something came up at home.

233
13:58.720 --> 13:59.630
Call me, okay?

234
13:59.630 --> 14:00.150
What the heck?

235
14:00.150 --> 14:01.200
I gotta go.

236
14:02.140 --> 14:05.630
[Emergency]

237
14:09.270 --> 14:11.000
What's with him?

238
14:12.840 --> 14:13.630
Three.

239
14:14.510 --> 14:15.320
Two.

240
14:16.230 --> 14:17.000
One.

241
14:44.000 --> 14:47.130
[West Gate]

242
14:47.130 --> 14:49.830
[Fucheng City Public Security Bureau Hospital Police Post]

243
15:11.550 --> 15:12.950
You were just gonna leave

244
15:13.320 --> 15:14.980
without so much as a word, huh?

245
15:16.510 --> 15:17.840
Here, you have the soda.

246
15:19.630 --> 15:20.600
I'll have a beer.

247
15:24.200 --> 15:25.000
Cheers.

248
15:26.510 --> 15:28.770
"Come, drink one last cup of wine with me.

249
15:28.840 --> 15:31.370
Beyond Yang Pass, no old friends you'll see."

250
15:32.000 --> 15:32.790
Cheers.

251
15:48.960 --> 15:50.840
Don't forget me when you get to the South.

252
15:50.840 --> 15:52.370
How could I ever forget you?

253
16:03.720 --> 16:04.790
I mean,

254
16:05.750 --> 16:06.950
you're very special.

255
16:08.000 --> 16:09.460
You're not easy to forget.

256
16:11.360 --> 16:12.240
I've never met

257
16:12.240 --> 16:13.500
anyone quite like you.

258
16:19.550 --> 16:20.880
What kind of person am I?

259
16:45.150 --> 16:46.510
I'm this kind of person.

260
17:02.720 --> 17:03.510
No.

261
17:04.000 --> 17:05.530
I'm going back to the South.

262
17:06.240 --> 17:09.440
Good, then I won't have to be responsible for you anymore.

263
17:13.589 --> 17:14.750
I-I'm very poor.

264
17:15.109 --> 17:16.550
Who freaking cares?

265
17:19.349 --> 17:20.410
I have a condition.

266
17:21.200 --> 17:22.460
I-I have a snow phobia.

267
17:30.000 --> 17:31.260
I have a condition too.

268
17:37.240 --> 17:38.200
I can't read.

269
17:54.240 --> 17:55.680
Are you sure you're taking the train?

270
17:54.520 --> 17:57.000
[East Zhanqian Road]

271
17:56.480 --> 17:58.410
Why not fly the day after tomorrow?

272
17:59.160 --> 18:00.440
The train's cheaper.

273
18:01.880 --> 18:02.400
Fine.

274
18:03.750 --> 18:04.750
I got the tickets.

275
18:04.880 --> 18:06.270
Check the tickets carefully.

276
18:06.270 --> 18:07.510
The first one gets you to

277
18:07.440 --> 18:08.600
[Fucheng to Nanjing]

278
18:07.510 --> 18:08.350
Nanjing tonight.

279
18:08.350 --> 18:10.070
The second one gets you to Fuzhou tomorrow.

280
18:08.600 --> 18:10.790
[Nanjing to Fuzhou]

281
18:10.070 --> 18:11.070
Don't mix them up.

282
18:14.240 --> 18:15.040
You're solid.

283
18:15.310 --> 18:16.200
Five stars, would use again.

284
18:16.200 --> 18:18.160
Together, they cost a little over 700 yuan.

285
18:18.160 --> 18:20.220
That's 300 yuan cheaper than flying.

286
18:20.680 --> 18:22.740
But that's 2 extra days of suffering.

287
18:22.750 --> 18:24.240
Three hundred isn't nothing.

288
18:24.240 --> 18:24.960
I've only managed to save up

289
18:24.960 --> 18:26.960
9,000 yuan over the past few months.

290
18:27.110 --> 18:28.240
Every little bit counts.

291
18:28.240 --> 18:29.270
Didn't Aunt Ling

292
18:29.270 --> 18:30.870
leave some money for you two?

293
18:32.000 --> 18:34.330
Zhengguang didn't give you yours, did he?

294
18:34.550 --> 18:35.440
He did.

295
18:35.510 --> 18:36.440
I didn't take it.

296
18:37.200 --> 18:38.790
You've learned to look out for your little brother.

297
18:38.790 --> 18:40.030
It's not that.

298
18:41.880 --> 18:42.680
At first, I was definitely

299
18:42.680 --> 18:44.010
going to take the money.

300
18:44.550 --> 18:46.280
But when I went home last night,

301
18:46.590 --> 18:48.450
I saw him eating instant noodles.

302
18:49.720 --> 18:51.120
You went home last night?

303
18:54.240 --> 18:55.570
What's wrong with that?

304
18:56.160 --> 18:56.960
Nothing.

305
18:57.000 --> 18:57.830
And then?

306
18:59.920 --> 19:00.590
Anyway,

307
19:00.590 --> 19:01.850
I just changed my mind.

308
19:02.640 --> 19:04.300
I'm leaving the money for him.

309
19:04.590 --> 19:06.650
You know what Liu Zhengguang is like.

310
19:06.790 --> 19:08.310
He's not the brightest and doesn't have much going for him.

311
19:08.310 --> 19:09.510
I'm afraid he won't find a job

312
19:09.510 --> 19:11.510
and will literally starve to death.

313
19:13.160 --> 19:15.220
You're being so generous, yet you're

314
19:15.720 --> 19:17.480
still trying to save money on airfare.

315
19:17.480 --> 19:19.410
I don't think you're saving money.

316
19:20.000 --> 19:21.930
I think you're dodging a debt, huh?

317
19:22.960 --> 19:24.070
Nonsense.

318
19:24.640 --> 19:26.100
How could I ever be in debt?

319
19:53.380 --> 20:04.630
[Contactless Payment; No Stopping Required]

320
20:04.240 --> 20:04.920
Be careful.

321
20:04.920 --> 20:07.180
No need to walk me any farther. I'm going.

322
20:07.200 --> 20:09.460
You're just trying to avoid Ai Chen, huh?

323
20:11.310 --> 20:12.240
No such thing.

324
20:13.310 --> 20:15.000
There's nothing between Ai Chen and me.

325
20:15.000 --> 20:16.510
We're just ordinary friends.

326
20:16.510 --> 20:17.310
No,

327
20:17.590 --> 20:18.920
just ordinary acquaintances.

328
20:18.920 --> 20:20.200
I haven't even asked you anything,

329
20:20.200 --> 20:22.530
and you're already giving yourself away.

330
20:28.790 --> 20:30.390
Alright, this is far enough.

331
20:30.750 --> 20:33.160
I'll keep in touch online once I get there.

332
20:34.720 --> 20:35.830
Once you leave,

333
20:37.240 --> 20:38.640
we'll go from colleagues

334
20:40.270 --> 20:41.730
and childhood friends...

335
20:42.880 --> 20:44.210
to just online friends.

336
20:49.270 --> 20:50.270
Take care.

337
21:07.270 --> 21:08.030
You too.

338
21:11.590 --> 21:12.920
-Everyone, tuck your feet in. -Thank you.

339
21:12.920 --> 21:14.110
-Thank you. -Thank you.

340
21:14.110 --> 21:14.880
Where're our berths?

341
21:14.880 --> 21:16.410
Excuse me, coming through.

342
21:16.830 --> 21:17.240
Here.

343
21:17.480 --> 21:17.830
This one?

344
21:17.830 --> 21:18.240
Here.

345
21:18.240 --> 21:19.170
Watch your feet.

346
21:19.720 --> 21:20.550
Excuse me.

347
21:22.510 --> 21:23.550
Whose shoes are these?

348
21:23.550 --> 21:24.350
Move them in a bit.

349
21:24.350 --> 21:25.750
Watch your feet. Thanks.

350
21:27.000 --> 21:27.880
Don't block the aisle.

351
21:27.880 --> 21:28.680
Okay, okay.

352
21:32.590 --> 21:33.750
Thanks. Come on.

353
21:38.070 --> 21:39.160
Okay, thanks.

354
21:39.160 --> 21:39.820
No problem.

355
21:41.960 --> 21:43.510
What, is your suitcase hard to push?

356
21:43.510 --> 21:44.350
Push harder.

357
21:44.550 --> 21:45.920
You're a man. Push harder.

358
21:45.920 --> 21:46.510
Okay, thanks.

359
21:46.510 --> 21:47.240
Okay, okay.

360
21:48.510 --> 21:49.710
Set it down securely.

361
21:52.310 --> 21:53.910
Everyone, pull your feet in.

362
21:56.200 --> 21:57.110
Liu Zhengliang is leaving today,

363
21:57.110 --> 21:57.920
you know?

364
21:58.110 --> 21:58.790
I know.

365
22:00.550 --> 22:02.400
He lied to me and said he was leaving tonight.

366
22:02.400 --> 22:03.510
I just called Junnan, and he said

367
22:03.510 --> 22:05.200
Zhengliang's already on the train now.

368
22:05.200 --> 22:05.790
What?

369
22:05.790 --> 22:07.590
You came j-just to tell me this?

370
22:10.510 --> 22:12.110
I was afraid you didn't know.

371
22:13.440 --> 22:15.370
What does it matter if I know or not?

372
22:15.400 --> 22:16.510
Was I supposed to throw myself on the floor, make a scene,

373
22:16.510 --> 22:17.270
and stop him from leaving?

374
22:17.270 --> 22:18.510
Why stop him?

375
22:19.000 --> 22:20.270
Didn't I tell you, Chen?

376
22:20.270 --> 22:21.270
You two aren't right for each other.

377
22:21.270 --> 22:22.440
Yeah, who could possibly be right

378
22:22.440 --> 22:23.400
for a guy like him?

379
22:23.400 --> 22:24.270
Exactly.

380
22:24.480 --> 22:25.310
The person who's right for him

381
22:25.310 --> 22:27.110
doesn't even exist in this world.

382
22:27.110 --> 22:28.510
He deserves to die alone.

383
22:28.590 --> 22:30.450
What did he say about me back then?

384
22:30.640 --> 22:32.640
He said I wasn't good enough for him.

385
22:34.030 --> 22:35.510
I'm not good enough for him?

386
22:35.510 --> 22:36.750
No, Chen, I was there that day.

387
22:36.750 --> 22:37.680
When h-he said that,

388
22:37.680 --> 22:38.310
I was there.

389
22:38.310 --> 22:38.680
Right.

390
22:38.680 --> 22:39.350
At the hospital.

391
22:39.350 --> 22:40.590
You were there.

392
22:40.590 --> 22:41.750
He said you weren't good enough for him.

393
22:41.750 --> 22:44.080
If you ask me, he's not good enough for you.

394
22:44.110 --> 22:45.550
You know, here's the thing:

395
22:45.550 --> 22:46.680
good looks have no ceiling,

396
22:46.680 --> 22:48.280
but insecurity has no floor.

397
22:48.510 --> 22:49.960
That's what I've been saying.

398
22:49.960 --> 22:51.560
He seems a bit insecure to me.

399
22:52.000 --> 22:52.790
Chen,

400
22:53.070 --> 22:54.680
you've hit the nail on the head.

401
22:54.680 --> 22:55.350
Right?

402
22:55.510 --> 22:57.200
People like him might seem

403
22:57.200 --> 22:58.270
cold and aloof on the outside,

404
22:58.270 --> 22:59.270
like they're full of confidence.

405
22:59.270 --> 23:01.480
But often, they're more insecure inside.

406
23:01.480 --> 23:02.270
Sometimes I wonder

407
23:02.270 --> 23:03.590
how to describe a guy like him.

408
23:03.590 --> 23:04.200
He's...

409
23:05.070 --> 23:05.920
He's just like tofu,

410
23:05.920 --> 23:06.680
you know?

411
23:08.720 --> 23:09.680
Such a pushover.

412
23:10.720 --> 23:11.920
Good thing he didn't go to school in the Northeast.

413
23:11.920 --> 23:12.590
If he had,

414
23:12.590 --> 23:13.720
he'd have been beaten up 8 times a day.

415
23:13.720 --> 23:14.640
Tell me about it.

416
23:14.640 --> 23:15.640
He's asking for a beating.

417
23:15.640 --> 23:16.750
He's begging for one.

418
23:16.750 --> 23:17.480
But you have to admit,

419
23:17.480 --> 23:18.720
he was a good student.

420
23:19.160 --> 23:20.270
So what if he was a good student?

421
23:20.270 --> 23:21.550
Does that make him better at taking a beating?

422
23:21.550 --> 23:23.350
He would get special treatment.

423
23:23.440 --> 23:25.440
Isn't that how it always is around here?

424
23:25.440 --> 23:26.240
True.

425
23:26.920 --> 23:28.550
E-Even so, he'd still get beaten up.

426
23:28.550 --> 23:29.610
He loved to snitch.

427
23:29.880 --> 23:30.810
What do you mean?

428
23:31.400 --> 23:33.310
Remember when we were kids and we'd make dumplings for the New Year?

429
23:33.310 --> 23:35.240
We'd put coins inside some of them.

430
23:35.240 --> 23:36.240
And I'd want to eat the ones with coins.

431
23:36.240 --> 23:37.680
So I'd poke them with chopsticks

432
23:37.680 --> 23:39.000
to find the hard ones.

433
23:39.000 --> 23:40.790
I'd poke them full of holes.

434
23:40.920 --> 23:42.270
Then he'd turn around and tell Mom.

435
23:42.270 --> 23:43.030
He did?

436
23:43.270 --> 23:45.200
Mom'd come back and give me a beating.

437
23:45.200 --> 23:46.350
You deserved it.

438
23:47.070 --> 23:48.160
That's true.

439
23:48.790 --> 23:50.240
But I used to do that too.

440
23:52.110 --> 23:53.160
Just poking them.

441
24:11.480 --> 24:12.920
Chen, when do you think

442
24:13.310 --> 24:14.770
he'll come back this time?

443
24:16.750 --> 24:17.750
Hard to say.

444
24:21.240 --> 24:22.480
Let him go if he wants to.

445
24:22.480 --> 24:24.010
As if anyone wants him back.

446
24:24.550 --> 24:26.030
How's your job hunt going?

447
24:27.720 --> 24:28.720
It's going great.

448
24:28.880 --> 24:31.030
Loads of people are fighting to hire me.

449
24:31.030 --> 24:32.510
I have to take my time to choose.

450
24:32.510 --> 24:33.910
Look at you, so in demand.

451
24:34.720 --> 24:37.050
Just don't get dazzled by all the options.

452
24:38.310 --> 24:40.110
If there's nothing else, I'll get going.

453
24:40.110 --> 24:40.920
Go on back.

454
24:41.110 --> 24:42.750
Drink some hot water. Don't catch a cold.

455
24:42.750 --> 24:43.480
It's pretty cold out here.

456
24:43.480 --> 24:44.480
I'll head inside in a bit.

457
24:44.480 --> 24:45.110
Bye-bye.

458
25:25.200 --> 25:26.310
You smoke?

459
25:29.680 --> 25:30.920
I started really young.

460
25:30.920 --> 25:32.180
But I don't smoke much.

461
25:32.640 --> 25:33.970
You didn't know I smoke?

462
25:34.590 --> 25:35.720
Never saw it before.

463
25:37.920 --> 25:38.830
You're not going to tell me

464
25:38.830 --> 25:39.750
that smoking is bad for my health

465
25:39.750 --> 25:41.480
and that I should quit, are you?

466
25:41.790 --> 25:43.310
Your body, your choice.

467
25:52.240 --> 25:54.110
But honestly, it's hard for me to imagine

468
25:54.110 --> 25:55.440
that in this day and age,

469
25:55.510 --> 25:57.970
there are still young people who can't read.

470
26:01.000 --> 26:02.460
I have a reading disorder.

471
26:04.240 --> 26:05.240
But it's not like

472
26:05.550 --> 26:07.480
I can't recognize any characters at all.

473
26:07.480 --> 26:08.640
I'd say I know about

474
26:08.640 --> 26:10.770
one-tenth of all Chinese characters.

475
26:11.350 --> 26:12.720
That sounds like

476
26:13.070 --> 26:15.200
abnormal neurological development.

477
26:16.270 --> 26:17.720
Have you ever seen a doctor about it?

478
26:17.720 --> 26:19.520
Other than that one time with me.

479
26:20.750 --> 26:21.880
I've had it checked.

480
26:22.960 --> 26:24.690
It's not a neurological issue.

481
26:25.070 --> 26:25.960
Then what is it?

482
26:36.640 --> 26:38.440
I dropped out in fifth grade.

483
26:39.160 --> 26:40.360
How is that possible?

484
26:41.310 --> 26:43.110
We have 9-year compulsory education.

485
26:43.110 --> 26:45.030
And we Northeasterners take education so seriously.

486
26:45.030 --> 26:46.890
My family situation was unusual.

487
26:48.400 --> 26:50.660
I didn't start third grade until I was 11.

488
26:52.440 --> 26:54.770
I've had trouble reading since I was a kid.

489
26:55.720 --> 26:57.030
So my parents were afraid I'd be

490
26:57.030 --> 26:58.510
-looked down on at school. -What's

491
26:58.510 --> 26:59.440
this character?

492
26:59.550 --> 27:01.160
So they taught me at home.

493
27:01.850 --> 27:08.290
[Be Late; After School; Home]

494
27:08.960 --> 27:10.960
I just taught you this yesterday,

495
27:11.240 --> 27:13.070
and you've already forgotten it?

496
27:13.070 --> 27:14.160
What's my name?

497
27:16.270 --> 27:18.830
What did we have for lunch?

498
27:20.880 --> 27:21.720
Rice.

499
27:22.790 --> 27:23.680
Smart girl.

500
27:23.880 --> 27:24.590
See?

501
27:25.160 --> 27:26.760
Then what's this character?

502
27:28.920 --> 27:29.830
Rice.

503
27:30.550 --> 27:31.480
Smart girl.

504
27:32.110 --> 27:32.920
Remember it.

505
27:34.590 --> 27:35.920
Write it a few more times.

506
27:35.920 --> 27:36.720
Ai San!

507
27:37.240 --> 27:38.310
Coming! Coming!

508
27:38.310 --> 27:39.920
Write it a-a few more times.

509
27:41.510 --> 27:42.310
Keep writing.

510
27:45.240 --> 27:46.100
Write it again.

511
27:47.720 --> 27:49.050
Do you know why I'm here?

512
27:53.000 --> 27:54.270
You dared to steal the antique

513
27:54.270 --> 27:56.240
belonging to a Hong Kong businessman?

514
27:56.240 --> 27:57.370
Where did you put it?

515
27:58.440 --> 27:59.640
B-Bring it out.

516
27:59.790 --> 28:01.000
That's a collectible.

517
28:01.000 --> 28:02.200
Worth a fortune.

518
28:04.680 --> 28:06.480
That was the first time I learned

519
28:08.200 --> 28:09.590
my mom had kleptomania.

520
28:10.960 --> 28:12.690
She couldn't control herself.

521
28:23.400 --> 28:24.680
Tell me, who did it?

522
28:24.680 --> 28:25.310
Me.

523
28:28.030 --> 28:29.890
With your hand injured like that,

524
28:30.030 --> 28:32.160
you still managed such delicate work?

525
28:33.310 --> 28:35.270
I-It didn't get in the way.

526
28:38.350 --> 28:39.210
Alright, then.

527
28:39.480 --> 28:40.740
You, come back with us.

528
28:41.640 --> 28:43.270
Ai Chen, I'm leaving.

529
28:46.160 --> 28:46.960
Dad!

530
28:52.590 --> 28:53.650
Listen to your mom.

531
28:54.680 --> 28:56.540
My dad went to jail just like that.

532
28:58.310 --> 29:00.160
The court ruled that the amount involved was huge,

533
29:00.160 --> 29:01.890
so he was sentenced to 10 years.

534
29:04.790 --> 29:08.110
Later, my mom got a job

535
29:08.790 --> 29:10.520
at a hospital through a friend,

536
29:10.590 --> 29:11.590
doing odd jobs.

537
29:14.400 --> 29:15.800
But she didn't last long.

538
29:16.110 --> 29:17.110
Her kleptomania acted up again,

539
29:17.110 --> 29:18.910
and they fired her immediately.

540
29:27.680 --> 29:28.480
Mi Si.

541
29:35.200 --> 29:36.000
She had no choice.

542
29:36.000 --> 29:37.070
She had to raise me.

543
29:38.480 --> 29:39.750
So she thought...

544
29:41.070 --> 29:42.440
why not go to the train station

545
29:42.440 --> 29:44.040
and return to her old tricks?

546
29:44.540 --> 29:46.510
[Passenger Travel Guidelines]

547
29:45.000 --> 29:46.270
Little did she know,

548
29:46.510 --> 29:47.090
[Our Service Promise]

549
29:47.680 --> 29:50.340
that the police had been watching her all along.

550
30:04.750 --> 30:05.810
And just like that,

551
30:06.960 --> 30:08.220
my mom went to jail too.

552
30:10.200 --> 30:11.480
I was left all alone,

553
30:11.640 --> 30:12.970
with no one to depend on.

554
30:15.030 --> 30:17.350
Uncle Li, the police officer,

555
30:18.720 --> 30:20.320
took pity on me and took me in.

556
30:21.590 --> 30:22.400
Xiaozhu?

557
30:22.720 --> 30:23.510
Xiaozhu.

558
30:25.310 --> 30:26.960
This is your sister, Chen.

559
30:27.640 --> 30:28.970
This is my son, Xiaozhu.

560
30:29.830 --> 30:31.360
Treat this as your own home.

561
30:48.310 --> 30:50.160
Hot dumplings coming up!

562
30:51.920 --> 30:52.640
Here.

563
30:53.160 --> 30:53.750
Alright.

564
30:54.160 --> 30:55.790
Eat slowly. Don't burn yourself.

565
30:55.790 --> 30:56.440
Come on.

566
30:56.790 --> 30:58.550
Try the dumplings I made.

567
30:59.310 --> 31:00.920
One for you. One for you.

568
31:01.440 --> 31:02.160
Eat up.

569
31:05.960 --> 31:08.290
Why wouldn't your mom let you go to school?

570
31:08.310 --> 31:10.720
She said learning at home was just as good.

571
31:11.310 --> 31:12.350
Nonsense.

572
31:13.270 --> 31:14.930
She was only holding you back.

573
31:24.310 --> 31:26.970
Xiaozhu, you've learned to take care of others.

574
31:27.200 --> 31:27.920
Eat up.

575
31:37.310 --> 31:38.160
Hand it over.

576
31:38.510 --> 31:40.070
Or we'll beat you up.

577
31:41.160 --> 31:42.000
Give it here.

578
31:42.000 --> 31:42.880
Hurry up!

579
31:44.200 --> 31:44.960
Hand it over.

580
31:44.960 --> 31:46.240
I'll say it again.

581
31:46.240 --> 31:48.100
Give it to us, or we'll beat you up!

582
31:48.160 --> 31:48.960
Hurry!

583
31:50.000 --> 31:50.790
Hurry up!

584
31:58.640 --> 31:59.480
You're asking for it.

585
31:59.480 --> 32:00.510
I'll kill you.

586
32:00.960 --> 32:01.750
Li Xiaozhu!

587
32:05.510 --> 32:06.310
This is my little brother.

588
32:06.310 --> 32:07.750
Get along well with him from now on,

589
32:07.750 --> 32:09.350
and I'll buy you more snacks.

590
32:10.200 --> 32:11.000
I want this one.

591
32:11.000 --> 32:11.680
This big one.

592
32:11.680 --> 32:11.960
Okay.

593
32:11.960 --> 32:12.680
Let's go.

594
32:14.310 --> 32:15.030
It's okay.

595
32:15.070 --> 32:16.920
From now on, Sis has your back.

596
32:19.790 --> 32:21.050
Come on, let's go home.

597
32:27.750 --> 32:29.810
Xiaozhu and I were both mischievous.

598
32:30.200 --> 32:31.000
Back then,

599
32:31.640 --> 32:33.100
he was my little sidekick.

600
32:33.680 --> 32:35.550
And me? I was the boss, naturally.

601
32:39.030 --> 32:40.960
He was in third grade,

602
32:41.480 --> 32:42.350
so Uncle Li

603
32:42.350 --> 32:43.550
put me straight

604
32:43.960 --> 32:45.160
into his class

605
32:45.160 --> 32:47.020
so we could go to school together.

606
32:49.200 --> 32:50.780
Strangely enough,

607
32:51.640 --> 32:53.640
I was very good at memorizing texts—

608
32:53.750 --> 32:55.680
classical poems and verses.

609
32:56.070 --> 32:57.480
I was okay at math too.

610
32:58.310 --> 33:00.040
But when it came to characters,

611
33:00.480 --> 33:02.160
I just couldn't remember them.

612
33:02.160 --> 33:02.920
So back then,

613
33:02.920 --> 33:04.200
both my teacher and Uncle Li thought

614
33:04.200 --> 33:06.330
I was deliberately refusing to learn.

615
33:06.350 --> 33:07.400
How could they have known

616
33:07.400 --> 33:09.060
that I had a reading disorder?

617
33:09.160 --> 33:11.070
But I didn't know at the time either.

618
33:11.070 --> 33:13.000
I only found out later, when I saw a doctor.

619
33:13.000 --> 33:15.160
The doctor said, "Why didn't you come earlier,

620
33:15.160 --> 33:16.360
when you were little?

621
33:16.720 --> 33:17.780
Now it's too late."

622
33:17.920 --> 33:18.640
Ai Chen,

623
33:18.640 --> 33:19.550
what's going on?

624
33:19.550 --> 33:21.550
Why aren't you doing your homework?

625
33:24.240 --> 33:25.900
Come to my office after class.

626
33:27.240 --> 33:28.030
Ai Chen,

627
33:28.720 --> 33:30.160
what's this character?

628
33:34.270 --> 33:35.400
What about this one?

629
33:39.720 --> 33:40.720
She can't read.

630
33:41.720 --> 33:42.720
She can't read.

631
33:42.830 --> 33:44.160
What did you just say?

632
33:46.030 --> 33:46.830
Beat him!

633
33:47.750 --> 33:49.880
No more bullying classmates at school!

634
33:49.880 --> 33:50.750
Do you hear me?

635
33:55.510 --> 33:56.510
And you.

636
33:57.550 --> 33:58.350
Child,

637
33:58.920 --> 34:00.680
if you don't study hard now,

638
34:01.000 --> 34:01.960
you definitely won't

639
34:01.960 --> 34:04.240
-get into college in the future. -It wasn't easy for Uncle Li to raise us.

640
34:04.240 --> 34:06.720
What will you do if you can't get into college?

641
34:06.720 --> 34:08.280
I was afraid that telling him I had a disorder

642
34:08.280 --> 34:09.480
would only cause him more trouble,

643
34:09.480 --> 34:10.679
so I kept it to myself.

644
34:11.920 --> 34:13.670
Later, the doctor told me

645
34:14.150 --> 34:16.080
that if we'd intervened in time...

646
34:20.070 --> 34:21.929
But there's no changing the past.

647
34:26.590 --> 34:27.590
Uncle Li...

648
34:29.070 --> 34:30.600
passed away very suddenly.

649
34:32.400 --> 34:33.710
After that,

650
34:34.280 --> 34:36.150
it was just Xiaozhu and me.

651
34:42.150 --> 34:42.920
Mentor!

652
34:43.360 --> 34:44.480
Mentor, wake up!

653
34:44.840 --> 34:45.590
Mentor!

654
34:48.110 --> 34:48.880
Mentor!

655
34:53.139 --> 34:54.340
[To Li Xiaofeng]

656
35:21.060 --> 35:24.340
[Forever in Our Hearts]

657
35:24.630 --> 35:25.590
Li Xiaozhu,

658
35:25.840 --> 35:27.030
stop crying.

659
35:27.920 --> 35:28.980
Hurry up and think—

660
35:29.000 --> 35:31.260
do you have any relatives you can rely on?

661
35:33.070 --> 35:33.710
Didn't you say

662
35:33.710 --> 35:35.030
your mom went to Shenzhen?

663
35:35.030 --> 35:36.630
Can you get in touch with her?

664
35:36.800 --> 35:37.590
I lied!

665
35:37.590 --> 35:39.590
I've never even met my mom!

666
35:39.590 --> 35:40.760
My dad said she ran off

667
35:40.760 --> 35:42.760
while working abroad that year!

668
35:42.760 --> 35:44.230
She'll never come back!

669
35:44.440 --> 35:45.630
Sis, are we going to

670
35:45.630 --> 35:47.440
have to beg for food from now on?

671
35:50.840 --> 35:51.920
Since you call me "Sis,"

672
35:51.920 --> 35:52.840
you won't starve

673
35:52.840 --> 35:54.040
as long as I have food.

674
36:00.000 --> 36:00.960
It's all packed.

675
36:00.960 --> 36:02.090
You can take it home.

676
36:02.510 --> 36:03.670
As for the expenses,

677
36:03.670 --> 36:05.000
Officer Zhang has already paid me.

678
36:05.000 --> 36:06.000
You don't need to worry about it.

679
36:06.000 --> 36:06.930
I'm heading out.

680
36:07.000 --> 36:07.920
Uncle Sun!

681
36:09.400 --> 36:10.150
Uncle Sun,

682
36:10.150 --> 36:11.750
I want to be your apprentice.

683
36:12.360 --> 36:13.150
My apprentice?

684
36:13.150 --> 36:14.400
What could I teach you?

685
36:14.400 --> 36:16.190
Teach me how to arrange funerals.

686
36:16.190 --> 36:17.050
Don't be silly.

687
36:17.400 --> 36:18.670
You're just a kid. You should be in school.

688
36:18.670 --> 36:19.480
Why get into the funeral business?

689
36:19.480 --> 36:20.630
You can't do this job.

690
36:20.630 --> 36:21.840
There are no adults left in our family.

691
36:21.840 --> 36:23.360
We have to support ourselves.

692
36:23.360 --> 36:25.070
People are always coming and going here,

693
36:25.070 --> 36:26.360
all crying and sobbing.

694
36:26.360 --> 36:27.840
Only you, hiding in the corner,

695
36:27.840 --> 36:28.630
look so happy.

696
36:28.630 --> 36:29.630
I don't.

697
36:30.510 --> 36:32.170
When you were counting money.

698
36:32.230 --> 36:33.510
I saw it all.

699
36:33.710 --> 36:34.710
I want to make money.

700
36:34.710 --> 36:35.280
I also want to

701
36:35.280 --> 36:37.140
be happy while others are crying.

702
36:38.630 --> 36:39.710
Don't talk nonsense here.

703
36:39.710 --> 36:41.000
This is serious work.

704
36:41.000 --> 36:42.230
What's all this talk about being happy?

705
36:42.230 --> 36:43.320
Uncle Sun.

706
36:46.800 --> 36:48.460
What can you do if I take you on?

707
36:50.230 --> 36:51.150
I can cry.

708
36:52.030 --> 36:53.800
Since you two will handle funerals for countless families,

709
36:53.800 --> 36:55.030
using your real names is not appropriate.

710
36:55.030 --> 36:55.840
I'll give you two

711
36:55.840 --> 36:57.570
stage names for this business.

712
36:57.760 --> 36:59.070
Li Xiaozhu, you're strong

713
36:59.070 --> 37:00.000
and chubby.

714
37:00.190 --> 37:01.710
And your real name means "Pillar."

715
37:01.710 --> 37:03.630
So from now on, you'll be "Rainbow Pillar."

716
37:03.630 --> 37:04.800
Ai Chen, you...

717
37:04.800 --> 37:05.480
Master,

718
37:05.630 --> 37:07.090
I'll keep my name, Ai Chen.

719
37:07.110 --> 37:08.440
Both your parents are still alive.

720
37:08.440 --> 37:09.800
Aren't you worried about bad luck?

721
37:09.800 --> 37:10.760
Every time I do this work,

722
37:10.760 --> 37:11.670
I sincerely hope

723
37:11.670 --> 37:13.800
the deceased will enjoy a good next life.

724
37:13.800 --> 37:14.840
You said it yourself:

725
37:14.840 --> 37:16.000
in our line of work,

726
37:16.150 --> 37:17.960
as long as you're sincere, there's no taboo

727
37:17.960 --> 37:19.890
to worry about and nothing to fear.

728
37:25.070 --> 37:26.470
Master, the food is here.

729
37:27.230 --> 37:28.630
Next time, I'll fetch it.

730
37:29.880 --> 37:30.590
Hurry, sit down and eat.

731
37:30.590 --> 37:31.550
Here, let's eat.

732
37:31.410 --> 37:34.710
♪ One who nestled close on a winter's night ♪

733
37:35.070 --> 37:38.260
♪ A bite of food beside a pool of gaze ♪

734
37:38.820 --> 37:40.940
♪ When summer dusk arrives ♪

735
37:41.380 --> 37:43.490
♪ We'll go to see the flowers ♪

736
37:45.980 --> 37:49.230
♪ One who was stranded on the road ♪

737
37:49.640 --> 37:52.770
♪ Heels buried under unseen snow ♪

738
37:50.280 --> 37:51.670
When I turned 18,

739
37:53.260 --> 37:55.500
♪ Don't panic—the journey is long ♪

740
37:53.280 --> 37:54.670
my master taught me

741
37:54.670 --> 37:55.670
everything he knew,

742
37:55.670 --> 37:56.590
and then he passed away too.

743
37:55.870 --> 37:58.390
♪ Long enough to hold your pause ♪

744
37:57.360 --> 37:59.070
After I saw him off on his final journey,

745
37:59.070 --> 37:59.840
I knew

746
38:01.440 --> 38:03.440
it was time to start my own business.

747
38:15.510 --> 38:17.320
1314 Funeral Services!

748
38:16.410 --> 38:20.700
[1314 Funeral Services]

749
38:30.530 --> 38:32.680
♪ Blows through the depths of winter ♪

750
38:31.430 --> 38:36.940
[Fucheng City Detention Center]

751
38:33.090 --> 38:35.890
♪ Stumbling along in the wind ♪

752
38:37.000 --> 38:39.570
♪ Flickering along in the wind ♪

753
38:40.670 --> 38:42.070
Later, my mom got out of prison.

754
38:41.150 --> 38:46.990
♪ Toward the crossroads brimming with sunlight ♪

755
38:42.550 --> 38:44.550
So she just started working with me.

756
38:45.510 --> 38:46.880
However, my mom

757
38:47.400 --> 38:48.590
has no interest

758
38:48.630 --> 38:49.960
in business at all.

759
38:50.320 --> 38:52.250
But she's really good at one thing:

760
38:52.510 --> 38:53.320
bargaining.

761
38:54.070 --> 38:55.360
So I brought her on board.

762
38:55.360 --> 38:57.590
I told her to be i-in charge of purchasing.

763
38:57.590 --> 38:58.920
She's really good at it.

764
38:59.590 --> 39:01.190
My dad is...

765
39:02.840 --> 39:04.670
very handy.

766
39:05.670 --> 39:06.960
So after he got out,

767
39:06.960 --> 39:08.590
he taught himself how to restore bodies,

768
39:08.590 --> 39:10.050
do their makeup, and so on.

769
39:10.760 --> 39:12.510
Xiaozhu and I handle the funeral ceremonies

770
39:12.510 --> 39:13.840
and play the suona horn—

771
39:14.000 --> 39:16.060
the whole one-stop funeral service.

772
39:17.510 --> 39:18.400
Now,

773
39:18.550 --> 39:21.080
business has been getting better and better.

774
39:22.150 --> 39:23.750
I really didn't expect this.

775
39:24.110 --> 39:25.550
I always assumed you just

776
39:26.070 --> 39:27.710
took over your father's business.

777
39:27.710 --> 39:29.770
Turns out, your father joined yours.

778
39:30.960 --> 39:32.360
You could put it that way.

779
39:35.760 --> 39:36.960
Does that bother you?

780
39:40.550 --> 39:41.750
What would bother me?

781
39:42.920 --> 39:43.920
Why do you think

782
39:43.920 --> 39:45.320
I'm telling you all this?

783
39:50.960 --> 39:51.920
I should go.

784
39:52.230 --> 39:53.290
Will you come back?

785
39:54.710 --> 39:55.440
No.

786
39:56.480 --> 39:58.340
We'll never see each other again?

787
39:58.550 --> 39:59.760
Probably not.

788
40:02.110 --> 40:03.440
When a-are you leaving?

789
40:03.960 --> 40:04.760
Tomorrow.

790
40:06.360 --> 40:08.670
I have a job tomorrow morning.

791
40:09.230 --> 40:10.230
If you're leaving after noon,

792
40:10.230 --> 40:11.290
I could see you off.

793
40:12.150 --> 40:13.190
It's okay. You don't have to.

794
40:13.190 --> 40:14.280
I'll go by myself.

795
40:15.710 --> 40:17.110
Will you remember me?

796
40:20.110 --> 40:21.110
Didn't I just answer

797
40:21.110 --> 40:22.230
that question?

798
40:28.360 --> 40:29.110
Go.

799
40:39.150 --> 40:40.280
You're so smart.

800
40:40.670 --> 40:41.920
You've learned so much

801
40:41.920 --> 40:44.150
just from watching TV and listening to the radio.

802
40:44.150 --> 40:45.550
That means you don't have

803
40:46.550 --> 40:47.550
a chronic

804
40:48.230 --> 40:49.800
neurodegenerative disease

805
40:49.800 --> 40:52.550
or vascular cognitive impairment.

806
40:53.070 --> 40:53.800
I think your disorder

807
40:53.800 --> 40:55.150
probably stems from a combination

808
40:55.150 --> 40:56.440
of childhood malnutrition,

809
40:56.440 --> 40:58.630
a difficult upbringing,

810
40:58.670 --> 41:01.730
psychological avoidance, and several other factors.

811
41:01.920 --> 41:03.320
Don't laugh. I'm serious.

812
41:03.320 --> 41:04.630
And look at you now.

813
41:04.670 --> 41:06.320
Your cognition and development

814
41:06.320 --> 41:07.510
are perfectly intact.

815
41:07.510 --> 41:08.710
So there's still a high chance

816
41:08.710 --> 41:10.710
that your condition can be treated.

817
41:12.550 --> 41:14.030
Aren't you something?

818
41:15.280 --> 41:18.280
You can tell I developed normally just by looking at me?

819
41:18.280 --> 41:19.110
Stop dragging this out, will you?

820
41:19.110 --> 41:20.710
If you're leaving, hurry up!

821
41:21.880 --> 41:23.810
Emotional wounds are hard to heal.

822
41:24.150 --> 41:25.810
You know that better than I do.

823
41:34.440 --> 41:35.240
You're right.

824
41:36.150 --> 41:37.410
I'm hardly one to talk.

825
41:59.000 --> 41:59.800
Young man.

826
42:00.800 --> 42:01.670
Young man!

827
42:03.590 --> 42:04.990
You're traveling alone?

828
42:07.550 --> 42:08.750
Where are you headed?

829
42:10.320 --> 42:11.230
The last stop.

830
42:11.960 --> 42:13.960
Going to Nanjing on a business trip?

831
42:14.230 --> 42:14.920
No.

832
42:15.280 --> 42:16.940
I'm going... going to Fuzhou.

833
42:17.280 --> 42:18.320
That's a long way.

834
42:18.760 --> 42:20.090
Must be a tough journey.

835
42:22.510 --> 42:24.480
What do you do for a living?

836
42:28.150 --> 42:29.320
I'm a doctor.

837
42:29.920 --> 42:31.150
You're a doctor?

838
42:31.360 --> 42:32.320
Which hospital?

839
42:33.000 --> 42:34.800
Fuzhou Kangtaierke Hospital.

840
42:36.630 --> 42:38.480
I know Contac.

841
42:39.150 --> 42:40.280
Kangtaierke?

842
42:40.760 --> 42:41.840
Never heard of it.

843
42:43.360 --> 42:44.920
So you're heading back

844
42:44.920 --> 42:46.190
after a business trip here.

845
42:46.190 --> 42:48.250
I thought you were a Northeasterner.

846
42:48.320 --> 42:49.980
Turns out you're from Fujian.

847
42:50.190 --> 42:52.320
I can't hear a trace of a Fujian accent.

848
42:52.510 --> 42:53.800
I'm not from Fujian.

849
42:55.110 --> 42:56.360
Then where are you from?
